      "text": "The generalized rule for divisibility by $11$ states that a number is divisible by $11$ if the difference between the sum of the digits at odd positions and the sum of the digits at even positions is divisible by $11$, with the last digit taken into account.\n\nFor the number $854\\boxed{n526}$, we have:\n\n\\[\n11(8 + 4 + 5 + 5 + n + 2 + 6) - (8 + n + 4 + 5 + 5 + 2 + 6) = 0\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify the equations:\n\n\\[\n11(30 + n) - (48 + n) = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\n40 + 10n - 48 - n = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\n9 + 9n = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\n9n = -9\n\\]\n\n\\[\nn = -1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, $\\boxed{-1}$ is the number we need.",
